    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0250" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/12174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-22T13:00:00+08:00">January 22, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>125. Reference my 1219, December 23, 9 p.m.,<anchor n="31" xml:id="d311-f1"/> and
                    my 1255, December 31, noon<anchor n="32" xml:id="d311-f2"/> regarding Wuhu
                    incidents. Having received no further reply showing satisfactory action to
                    locate the military unit concerned, I have again brought the matter to the
                    attention of the Japanese Consul General asking that it be referred to his
                    military authorities for prompt and satisfactory action.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
